Subject: [PATCH 05/18] Plutonium: the browser panel on Plutonium's browser
 tabs

In the Plutonium shell (navigator.windowBroker with tabs), T3's browser
works without Electron:

- plutonium/previewBridge.ts implements DesktopPreviewBridge on the
  broker's tabs, tagged with their thread id. What a page opens loads in
  the same tab, as in Electron. A reload of the shell adopts its tabs.
- plutonium/PlutoniumBrowserHost.tsx shows each session's tab with a
  SurfaceEmbed <embed> where the panel or mini player wants it, at the
  session's viewport (scaled to fit), invisibly while an agent works in it
  in the background, and draws the page's alert/confirm/prompt.
- previewBridge and isPreviewSupportedInRuntime accept the Plutonium shell.

Not yet: zoom, color scheme, element picking, screenshots to file,
recording, picture-in-picture windows, cookie import, DevTools window.

